comments.body:
I removed it to keep the package in line with the "official" way of loading diagrams. 

_This needs to be handled in documentation, but we first need the API to be stable._

We should make it clear that the only thing needed in an external diagram is the `ExternalDiagramDefinition`. The extra imports aren't useful to anyone who just wants to add an external diagram. 
In case anyone really wants to access them, they can simply use `const {id, detector, loader} = mindmap`.

Also, when there is more than one diagram, the import statement gets ugly. I'm usually not a fan of default exports, but this is one scenario where it makes sense. 

```js
import {
  loader as mindmapLoader, detector as mindmapDetector, id as mindmapId
} from "@mermaid-js/mermaid-mindmap";
```

```js
import mindmap from "@mermaid-js/mermaid-mindmap";
// mindmap.id
// mindmap.loader
// mindmap.detector
```
